  "title": "Checkerboard m-sequence-based c-VEP dataset from",
  "description": "A derivative EEG dataset containing checkerboard m-sequence-based code-modulated visual evoked potential (c-VEP) recordings from 16 healthy participants across 8 sessions. The dataset evaluates the influence of spatial frequency in visual stimuli for brain-computer interface applications, with 16-channel EEG data sampled at 256 Hz and annotated with HED 8.4.0 tags for standardized event representation.",
  "methods_description": "EEG data were acquired from 16 channels using a standard 1005 montage at a sampling rate of 256 Hz with 50 Hz line frequency filtering. Participants completed 8 sessions with 3 runs per session (2 training, 1 testing), viewing checkerboard m-sequence-based visual stimuli in a c-VEP paradigm with 2 classes.",
